{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2soil1a","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"coordination-compounds","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"warners-theory-and-valence-bond-theory","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pamong-the-following-complexes-k-pp-pksub3sub-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-yzu7puwkdr32r6ai","content":"<p>Among the following complexes (K-P),</p>\n<p>K<sub>3</sub>[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>] (K), [Co(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>6</sub>]Cl<sub>3</sub> (L), Na<sub>3</sub>[Co(oxalate)<sub>3</sub>] (M), [Ni(H<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>3</sub>]Cl<sub>2</sub> (N), K<sub>2</sub>[Pt(CN)<sub>4</sub>] (O) and [Zn(H<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>6</sub>(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>] (P)</p>\n<p>The diamagnetic complexes are</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"K, L, M, N"},{"identifier":"B","content":"K, M, O, P"},{"identifier":"C","content":"L, M, O, P"},{"identifier":"D","content":"L, M, N, O"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>In K<sub>3</sub>Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub> :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 32 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtmjor/6e6a379c-9ec6-495f-a808-ae1a6af5ce7e/73cbafb0-6537-11ef-bb89-99be14e66686/file-jaoe38c1m0dtmjos.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>CN<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> being a strong field ligand, it causes pairing of electrons, so only one unpaired electron. The complex is paramagnetic.</p>\n<p>In Co[(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>6</sub>]Cl<sub>3</sub> :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dto8d6/06eac3d2-bed5-4f96-b871-975aaa91a5b3/a2ab0ba0-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dto8d7.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m0dto8d6/06eac3d2-bed5-4f96-b871-975aaa91a5b3/a2ab0ba0-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dto8d7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\