h:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 32 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtq76w/90382aec-a23e-4f1d-acb6-3ade9745766d/d9611680-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtq76x.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m0dtq76w/90382aec-a23e-4f1d-acb6-3ade9745766d/d9611680-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtq76x.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtq76w/90382aec-a23e-4f1d-acb6-3ade9745766d/d9611680-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtq76x.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtq76w/90382aec-a23e-4f1d-acb6-3ade9745766d/d9611680-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtq76x.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtq76w/90382aec-a23e-4f1d-acb6-3ade9745766d/d9611680-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtq76x.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtq76w/90382aec-a23e-4f1d-acb6-3ade9745766d/d9611680-6537-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtq76x.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Oxalate being a strong field ligand  it causes pairing of electron spins. There is no unpaired electron, hence the complex is diamagnetic.</p>\n<p>In [Ni(H<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>6</sub>]Cl<sub>2</sub> :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 32 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m0dts0uo/22e4c562-6980-4dc4-aaac-b4c222533bd4/0c19b500-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dts0up.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Since H<sub>2</sub>O is a weak field ligand, no pairing takes place. There are two unpaired electrons, so the complex is paramagnetic.</p>\n<p>In K<sub>2</sub>[Pt(CN)<sub>4</sub>] :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 32 English Explanation 5\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m0dtt7hm/8816af01-c41e-4288-8cbf-f0c89cff47c7/2d098fb0-6538-11ef-8abf-559c8ea7060f/file-jaoe38c1m0dtt7hn.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>CN<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> being a strong field ligand, it causes pairing of electrons spins, so no unpaired electron. Hence, the complex is diamagnetic.</p>\n<p>In [Zn(H<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>6</sub>(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>] : Zn<sup>2+</sup> has 3d<sup>10</sup> configuration. Therefore, it is a diamagnetic complex.</p>"}]}